# atelier canonical allowed_signers — the fleet's single trust list for git
# commit/tag signature verification (SIGNING.md, ADR 0007).
#
# One-fact-one-home (EVIDENCE §9): signing trust has exactly one source. Machines
# point git config here; child CI resolves it at the child's existing atelier pin
# (ADR 0002), never floating main — a floated trust list would let anyone with
# write access to main mint trust for every child silently.
#
# Public keys only — safe in a public repo. APPEND-ONLY: a retired key is bounded
# with valid-before, never deleted, so old signatures stay verifiable forever
# (git verifies against the commit's own committer timestamp).
#
# Values are QUOTED: the man page's unquoted valid-after form fails to parse on
# macOS OpenSSH ("missing start quote"), and a parse failure silently fails the
# whole entry — see SIGNING.md.
#
# Timestamps carry an explicit "Z" (UTC) suffix and sit BEFORE the earliest
# signed commit's committer time in UTC. Without the suffix ssh-keygen reads the
# date in the verifier's LOCAL timezone, so the same list passes on a UTC+12
# machine and fails in a UTC CI runner ("key is not yet valid") — a commit made
# at 02:13 NZST is 14:13 the PREVIOUS UTC day. UTC-anchor the window and the two
# planes agree. (Caught by atelier's own CI dogfood 2026-07-12.)
